---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { archivedDocuments } from '../data/documents';
import { KIND_LABELS } from '../data/schemas/documents';

/**
 * A deliberate gap page.
 *
 * Who holds office and how to reach each office are the two things residents
 * most often want, and they are exactly what this project cannot currently
 * source to its own standard. Saying so plainly, and saying where to look
 * instead, is more useful than a confident page that might be wrong.
 */

const officeDocuments = archivedDocuments.documents
  .filter((doc) => doc.kind === 'office-document' || doc.kind === 'citizens-charter')
  .sort((a, b) => (b.publishedYear ?? 0) - (a.publishedYear ?? 0) || a.title.localeCompare(b.title));

const latestOfficeYear = Math.max(...officeDocuments.map((doc) => doc.publishedYear ?? 0));
const age = new Date().getUTCFullYear() - latestOfficeYear;
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Government', href: '/government' }];
---

<Base
  title="Government of Calatagan"
  description="Who holds municipal office in Calatagan, Batangas, and how to reach each office — what can and cannot yet be verified from primary sources, and where to look instead."
  {crumbs}
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Government"
    title="Who governs Calatagan — and what we can prove"
    lede="Who holds office and how to reach each office are what residents ask for most. They are also the two things this project cannot yet establish to its evidence standard, so this page sets out the gap instead of filling it with a plausible guess."
    {crumbs}
  />

  <div class="container page-body">
    <nav class="on-page" aria-label="On this page">
      <a href="#officials">Elected officials</a>
      <a href="#contacts">Offices and contacts</a>
      <a href="#archive">What the archive holds</a>
      <a href="#reach">Reaching the municipality today</a>
    </nav>

    <section class="section prose" id="officials" aria-labelledby="officials-title">
      <h2 id="officials-title">Elected officials</h2>
      <p>
        Calatagan elects a Mayor, a Vice Mayor and eight members of the Sangguniang Bayan. The May
        2025 local elections have been held and the results are a matter of public record.
      </p>
      <div class="callout clay">
        <p class="callout-title">Why the roster is not published here</p>
        <p>
          <em>An election result is not proof of present incumbency.</em> Between an election and
          today, an officeholder can resign, be suspended, be disqualified, die, or be succeeded.
          Publishing election winners as current officials asserts something the election return
          does not say.
        </p>
      </div>
      <h3>What we would need to publish it</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          A Commission on Elections certificate of canvass or official published return, rather
          than media reporting of the count.
        </li>
        <li>
          A current roster from the Department of the Interior and Local Government or its
          municipal field office, confirming who is in office now.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Neither is currently reachable. COMELEC’s published attachment directories return errors to
        this project’s tooling, and DILG publishes no machine-readable municipal roster we have
        found. Election results are available from civic-tech derivatives of COMELEC data and from
        news organisations; both are useful for finding the answer and neither is sufficient to
        publish it.
      </p>
      <p class="small muted">
        Tracked as an open item in <a href="/sources#withheld">Sources</a>. If you have a primary
        document, a correction with a citation is welcome.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section prose" id="contacts" aria-labelledby="contacts-title">
      <h2 id="contacts-title">Offices and contact details</h2>
      <p>
        A telephone number, an e-mail address and a postal address for the municipal hall circulate
        on a national government portal. We do not republish them as current, and the reason is
        worth stating precisely.
      </p>
      <p>
        Those contact details sit in a single record submitted by the LGU to that portal. Three
        other fields in the same record — the municipality’s income classification, the name of its
        mayor, and its website address — are all demonstrably out of date. The income
        classification is two years stale; the website it lists no longer resolves at all. Contact
        details drawn from the same record, of the same vintage, cannot be presented as current
        simply because they are the only ones available.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Publishing a wrong phone number has a real cost.</strong> Someone travels to an
        office that has moved, or calls a line nobody answers, and concludes the information was
        checked when it was not.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="archive" aria-labelledby="archive-title">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2 id="archive-title">What the archive holds</h2>
        <p>
          The municipality’s former website published a set of {officeDocuments.length} per-office
          documents, most of them in {latestOfficeYear}. A sample has been opened: they are
          <strong>Citizen’s Charter service standards</strong> in the Anti-Red Tape Authority format
          — each service listing its requirements, fees and processing times.
        </p>
        <div class="callout warn">
          <p class="callout-title">Archived, not current</p>
          <p>
            The {latestOfficeYear} set is {age} years old. A fee or a processing time from it is a
            starting point for a question at the municipal hall, never an answer. This site does not
            restate any of those figures — nor the e-mail addresses and telephone numbers in the
            one-page <em>List of Offices</em>, which the only other record of them cannot confirm.
            The document is linked below so you can judge its age for yourself.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="table-wrap" role="region" aria-labelledby="office-caption" tabindex="0">
        <table class="stack">
          <caption id="office-caption">
            Per-office documents from the former municipal website ({officeDocuments.length})
          </caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Document</th>
              <th scope="col">Kind</th>
              <th scope="col">Published</th>
              <th scope="col">Archived copy</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {officeDocuments.map((doc) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{doc.title}</th>
                <td data-label="Kind">{KIND_LABELS[doc.kind]}</td>
                <td data-label="Published">{doc.publishedYear ?? '—'}</td>
                <td data-label="Archived copy">
                  <a href={doc.archiveUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow">
                    Open<span class="visually-hidden"> {doc.title} on the Wayback Machine</span>
                    <span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span>
                  </a>
                </td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="small muted prose">
        Entries a maintainer has actually opened carry a note saying what was found inside; the rest
        are described by the filename the municipality chose. All of them appear in the
        <a href="/documents">archive</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section prose" id="reach" aria-labelledby="reach-title">
      <h2 id="reach-title">If you need to reach the municipality today</h2>
      <p>
        Go in person to the municipal hall, or contact the Provincial Government of Batangas, which
        maintains current contact routes to its municipalities. This project would rather send you
        to a source that is current than to one of its own that might not be.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-body {
    padding-block: var(--sp-6) var(--sp-8);
  }
  .on-page {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--sp-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-6);
  }
  .on-page a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: var(--tap);
    padding: 0 var(--sp-4);
    border: var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--c-surface);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .on-page a:hover {
    border-color: var(--c-accent);
  }
  .section {
    scroll-margin-top: var(--sp-5);
  }
  .callout {
    margin-block: var(--sp-5);
  }
  th[scope='row'] {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
